  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "Parties and defined names",
    "text": "This Agreement is made by and between the CITY OF YOUNGSTOWN, OHIO (hereinafter the \"City\") and HARDRIVES PAVING & CONSTRUCTION, INC. (hereinafter “Hardrives”), an Ohio corporation."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "1. License Grant",
    "text": "1. The City agrees to grant to Hardrives a license for use of the property, including, but not limited io, fixtures, existing improvements, and appurtenant structures thereon, all located within the City and described more fully in the attached Exhibit A (hereinafter the \"Premises\")."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "2. Use",
    "text": "2. Use. The City and Hardrives agree that the Premises will be declared surplus property and deemed not needed for public use by the Director of Finance and is to be used in connection with economic development purposes. Hardrives intends to utilize the Premises for the production, distribution, and sale of paving materials and other similar products and for the operation of its management and corporate offices. The Premises will further be used for the storage and operation of all equipment, personal property, and supplies necessary for said purposes."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "3. Rental",
    "text": "3. Rental. Hardrives agrees to pay to the City a rental fee of one dollar ($1.00) per year."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "4. Event of Default",
    "text": "4, Event of Default. Failure to make annual payments within thirty (80) days of the date payment is due shall constitute an event of default. Upon written notice by the City, Hardrives shall have ten (10) days, within which to cure such default. If said default is not cured within that ten (10) day period: following notice from the City, Hardrives shall be held to have breached this Agreement and shall surrender all rights to the use of the Premises."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "5. Terms",
    "text": "5. Terms. This Agreement shall continue: (1) for a term of one (1) year from the date of execution of this Agreement; or (2) until the date that title to the Premises is conveyed and transferred to Hardrives by the City, pursuant to a Development Agreement entered into by and between the City and Hardrives, regarding the Premises, which shall be entered into on or before December 31, 1999."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "6.A City Authorization",
    "text": "A. As of the date hereof, and on the date of the execution, delivery, and performance of this Agreement, the Board of Control for the City has been duly authorized by the City Council to enter into this Agreement, and this Agreement constitutes a valid and binding obligation of the City."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "6.B City Authority and Premises Claims",
    "text": "B. The City has full authority to license the use of the Premises and said Premises shall be clear of all liens and claims of any party, except for easements of record, any and all unrecorded easements identified by the City prior to the execution of this Agreement, rights of way, and access rights appurtenant to the Center Street Bridge and access ramps thereto. Further, the City is not in default under any law or regulation or under any order of any court or federal, state, or municipal or other governmental department, commission, board, bureau, agency, or instrumentality affecting the Premises. Finally, there are no claims, actions, suits, or proceedings instituted, filed or threatened, which may affect the Premises."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "6.C Easements and Rights of Way",
    "text": "C. This license to Hardrives by the City will include the right to use all easements and right of ways, as may be necessary to have access to, and utilization of, the Premises."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "6.D Environmental Warranty",
    "text": "D. The Premises has never, and does not currently contain, nor is it contaminated by, any hazardous or toxic waste materials, except as set forth in the Environmental Site Assessment Phase | and If report attached hereto as Exhibit B, in violation of any applicable environmental laws or regulations, including, but not limited to, Section 103 of the Comprehensive Environmental Response, Compensation and Liability Act, 42 U.S.C. D9601 et seq. and Chapter 3734 of the Ohio Revised Code. Further, no “clean-up” of the Premises has occurred pursuant to any applicable federal or state environmental laws or regulations, which would give rise to (i) liability on the part of any person, entity, or association to reimburse any governmental authority for the costs of such “clean-up,” or (ii) a lien or encumbrance on the Premises."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "7.A Hardrives Authorization",
    "text": "A. As of the date hereof, and on the date of the execution and performance of this Agreement, Hardrives has been duly authorized to enter into this Agreement, and this Agreement constitutes a valid and binding obligation of Hardrives."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "7.B Waste and Surrender of Premises",
    "text": "B. Hardrives agrees to lay no waste to the Premises during the term of its use of the Premises and to surrender the Premises to the City upon termination of this Agreement in as good a condition as received, normal wear and tear and damage due to casualty excepted."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "7.C Insurance",
    "text": "C. During the term of this Agreement, Hardrives shall maintain a policy of insurance in the amount of $1,000,000.00 to include comprehensive liability coverage naming the City, as an additional insured of said policy. Hardrives shall maintain worker's compensation insurance on its employees and shall provide the City with a certificate thereof."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "7.D Hazardous Materials and Environmental Compliance",
    "text": "D. Hardrives shall use all precautions necessary to ensure against the creation, use, or storage of any hazardous material or waste on the Premises. Hardrives agrees that, during its use of the Premises, Hardrives will comply with Environmental Protection Agency laws or regulations in effect presently or enacted during the term of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "7.E Indemnity",
    "text": "E. Hardrives agrees to hold harmless the City against any and all claims, liabilities, damages, and losses, including expenses incidental to the defense of same, resulting from injury on or about the Premises or in conjunction with Hardrives’ use and occupancy of the Premises."
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "7.F Legal Compliance",
    "text": "F. All work performed on the Premises shall be in conformity with all applicable federal, state, and local laws and regulations."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "8. As-Is Condition",
    "text": "8. Hardrives acknowledges that it is accepting the Premises in its \"as is\" condition, without any express or implied warranty of the condition of the Premises, apart from warranties and representations made by the City, which are contained in this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "9. Entire Agreement",
    "text": "9. This Agreement, and the documents delivered pursuant hereto, constitute the entire Agreement and understanding between the parties hereto."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "9. Written Amendments",
    "text": "This Agreement may be modified or amended only by a duly authorized written instrument executed by the parties hereto."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "9. Assignment",
    "text": "This Agreement is not assignable by either party without the written consent of the other party."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "10. Governing Law",
    "text": "10. This Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the State of Ohio."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "11. Survival",
    "text": "11. All warranties, covenants, representations, and guarantees shall survive the execution and delivery of this Agreement and any other documents contemplated by the Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "12. Defined Parties",
    "text": "12. The terms \"City\" and “Hardrives,\" as both are used herein, shall include all persons so designated and their heirs, executors, administrators, successors, and assigns."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "Exhibit A. Premises Description",
    "text": "The “Premises,” as set forth in this License Agreement, shall include, but is not limited to, the property designated as Parcel No. 3 in the Quit Claim Deed from the LTV Steel Company, Inc., as Grantor, to the City of Youngstown, Ohio, as Grantee, dated May 4, 1994, and recorded in the Mahoning County Recorder's Office on May 26, 1994 at Mahoning County Official Records 2263, Page 1. Parcel No. 3, contained in said Quit Claim Deed, at Mahoning County Official Records 2263, Pages 10-12, is more fully set forth as follows: Parcel No. 3: SITUATED in the part in the City of Youngstown and in part in the city of Campbell, County of Mahoning, State of Ohio and known as being all of Out Lots 685, 686, 688 and parts of Out Lot 186, 187, 680 and 683 of the present numbering system of the City of Youngstown, and also known as being a part of original Great Lot 25 in the original survey of Coitsville Township now located in the City of Campbell, and is further bounded and described as follows: Beginning at a point in the centerline of the Mahoning River at its intersection with the westerly line of lands now or formerly owned by the Pittsburgh, Youngstown and Ashtabula Railroad Co. now owned by Conrail, said point being S. 36° -00’ E., 167.20 feet from an iron pin set near the northerly bank of Mahoning River; Thence northwesterly up the centerline of the Mahoning River on a curve to the right, said curve having a radius of 600.00 feet, an arc of 658.75 feet and a chord bearing N. 75° -51’ -30” W., 658.73 feet to a point; Thence N. 42° -33’ -50” W. continuing along the centerline of the Mahoning River 3250.00 feet to a point; 7 Thence N. 64° -06’ —55” W. continuing along the centerline of the Mahoning River 785.81 feet to a point at its intersection with the easterly line of lands owned by the B & O Railroad, said point also being S. 3° -20’ -25” W., 120.00 feet from an iron pin set near the east bank of the Mahoning River: Thence N. 3° -20’ —25” E. along the easterly line of lands of the B & O Railroad 180.00 feet to _ an iron pin set; Thence along the southerly line of lands of the B & O Railroad, the following four courses: N. 58° -41' -35” W., 468.00 feet to an iron pin set; Northerly along a curve to the right, said curve having a radius of 1903.08 feet, an arc of 582.37 feet, and a chord bearing N. 49° -55’ —35” W., a distance of 580.10 feet to an iron pin set; N. 41° -09’ —35” W., 304.40 feet to an iron pin set; Northerly along a curve to the right, said curve having a radius of 570.65 feet, an arc of 296.71 feet and a chord bearing N. 26° -15' —-50” W., a distance of 293.39 feet to an iron pin set; Case: 4:04-cv-01817-GJL Doc #: 125-21 Filed: 03/10/10 6 of 14. PagelD #: 1838 Thence along the southerly and westerly lines of the lands of the B & O Railroad and the Conrail Railroad, the following nineteen courses: S. 36° -24' -35” E., 30.20 feet to an iron pin set; Along a curve to the left, said curve having a radius of 564.41 feet, an arc of 258.55 feet, and a chord bearing S. 27° -56’ —10” E. a distance of 256.29 feet to an iron pin set; S. 41° -03’ -35” E., 183.75 feet to an iron pin set; Along a curve to the left, said curve having a radius of 287.94 feet, an arc of 110.64 feet, and a chord bearing S. 52° -04’ -05” E. a distance of 109.96 feet to an iron pin set: S. 63° -04’ -35” E., 65.56 feet to an iron pin set; N. 26° -55’ —25” E., 14.62 feet to an iron pin set; S. 63° -04' ~35” E., 90.00 feet to an iron pin set; S. 67° -29’ -05” E., 300.89 feet to an iron pin set; S. 63° -04’ -35” E., 300.00 feet to an iron pin set; S. 56° -24' -35” E., 201.36 feet to an iron pin set; S. 63° -04’ ~35” E., 100.00 feet to an iron pin set; S. 33° -04’ ~50” E., 42.25 feet to an iron pin set; S. 71° -14’ -35” E., 965.49 feet to an iron pin set; Along a curve to the right, said curve having a radius of 369.34 feet, an arc of 158.36 feet and a chord bearing S. 58° -58' -05” E., a distance of 157.05 feet to an iron pin set: S. 46° -41’ -35” E., 100.00 feet to an iron pin set; S. 43° -26' -35” E., 276.18 feet to an iron pin set; S. 44° -47’ -05” E., 863.28 feet to an iron pin set; S. 61° -39’ -50” E., 95.16 feet to an iron pin set; S. 36° -00’ E., 2361.45 feet to the place of beginning, as appears by said plat, be the same more or less, but subject to all legal highways. And containing within said bounds a total of 58.086 acres of land of which 2.34 acres are contained within the City of Campbell and of the total acreage 8.1+ acres are contained within the Mahoning River, according to a survey by Lynn, Kittinger & Noble, Inc., Professional Surveyors, by Carroll L. Herrmann, P.S. Ohio # 5663, December, 1992."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "Exhibit A. Parcel Exceptions",
    "text": "Excepting from Parcel No. 3, as set forth above, the following: 1. A 1.102 acre parcel of land conveyed to CSX, Transportation, inc., by Deed recorded in Volume 2430, Page 336, Mahoning County Official Records; 2. A 65,781 square foot parcel of land conveyed to Mahoning County by Deed recorded in Volume 3157, Page 319, Mahoning County Official Records; and 3. A 357 square foot parcel of land conveyed to Mahoning County by Deed recorded in Volume 3157, Page 322, Mahoning County Official Records."
  }
