   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The grant describes the licensed property as \"including, but not limited to, fixtures, existing improvements, and appurtenant structures\" and defers to Exhibit A, so the outer boundary of the \"Premises\" is left open-ended against enumerated specifics. A court could be asked whether anything beyond the listed items and the Exhibit A parcel is licensed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42},
     {"issue": "The open-ended grant sits against Exhibit A, which itself says the Premises \"shall include, but is not limited to\" a precise metes-and-bounds Parcel No. 3, so neither document fixes what land is covered. The two open-ended descriptions compound rather than resolve each other.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Hardrives intends to utilize the Premises for ... paving materials and other similar products\" is drafted as a statement of intent, not a covenant, leaving it unclear whether it limits permitted use at all, and \"other similar products\" has no fixed boundary. A court could be asked whether a given activity is a permitted use or a breach.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.40},
