   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The written word and the numeral disagree: \"thirty (80) days,\" so the cure/default trigger period is internally contradictory on its face. A court would have to decide whether thirty or eighty days governs the event of default.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The term \"shall continue: (1) for a term of one (1) year ... or (2) until the date that title ... is conveyed\" joins two inconsistent measures with \"or\" and gives no rule for which controls, so it is unclear whether the licence expires after a year or runs until conveyance. It also does not say what happens if the contemplated Development Agreement is never entered into by December 31, 1999.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.57},
     {"issue": "The clause presupposes a separate Development Agreement conveying title, yet paragraph 9 declares this Agreement and documents delivered pursuant to it the entire agreement, leaving the relationship between the two instruments unresolved. A court could be asked whether the licence survives once the Development Agreement path fails.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.12},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The warranty that the Premises \"shall be clear of all liens and claims of any party\" is qualified by an enumerated list of exceptions (easements of record, unrecorded easements identified by the City, rights of way, Center Street Bridge access rights) whose reach is uncertain, particularly \"any and all unrecorded easements identified by the City prior to the execution.\" Whether an unlisted encumbrance falls inside or outside the carve-out is a construction question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.38},
     {"issue": "The flat statement that \"there are no claims, actions, suits, or proceedings ... which may affect the Premises\" is hard to square with paragraph 6.D's acknowledgement of conditions disclosed in the Exhibit B environmental assessment and with Exhibit A's excepted conveyances to CSX and Mahoning County. A court could be asked whether those disclosures qualify this warranty.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.34}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"All easements and right of ways, as may be necessary to have access to, and utilization of, the Premises\" fixes no identified easements and no standard of necessity, so its scope is indeterminate. A court would have to decide what access rights the licence actually conveys.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.36},
     {"issue": "This grant of \"all easements and right of ways ... necessary\" sits awkwardly against paragraph 6.B, which excepts rights of way and access rights appurtenant to the Center Street Bridge and ramps from the City's clear-title warranty. The two provisions point in opposite directions on the same access rights.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.31}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The syntax buries the qualifier: the Premises has never contained hazardous materials \"except as set forth in the Environmental Site Assessment ... in violation of any applicable environmental laws or regulations,\" so it is unreadable whether the warranty is of no contamination at all, no contamination beyond the report, or only no unlawful contamination. That misplaced modifier is the whole measure of the City's environmental exposure.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.63},
     {"issue": "The exception incorporates the Exhibit B Phase I/II assessment, which describes \"Parcel No. 3\" as a 5.44-acre site within a 123.07-acre study area, while Exhibit A's Parcel No. 3 is a 58.086-acre tract from the LTV quit claim deed. The disclosure document and the definition of the Premises do not describe the same land, so the scope of the carve-out cannot be fixed from the instrument.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.48}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.06},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Lay no waste\" and return \"in as good a condition as received, normal wear and tear and damage due to casualty excepted\" set no measurable baseline for a contaminated former steel site. What condition the Premises was \"received\" in is precisely what the parties would dispute.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.36},
     {"issue": "The obligation to surrender the Premises substantially unaltered is hard to reconcile with paragraph 2, which contemplates industrial production, distribution and storage of paving materials and equipment on the site. A court could be asked whether use authorised by paragraph 2 can constitute waste under this paragraph.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.12},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.08}
   ]}
]}

